## Usage

All 30 motion components are organized below into 11 dedicated category bands. Use the sticky category bar to jump directly to any group, and interact via hover, focus, click, drag or variant switches. The reset button remounts only that specimen, restoring local models and playback; clicking any component name opens its full variant gallery and API page.

::DocsComponentsGallery{suite="motion"}
::

### Best Practices

- Drive values, items, status and navigation from your application. A visual press, loading cycle or submit request does not establish that a business operation succeeded.
- Keep repeated or decorative motion out of live regions. Provide one readable text value and native keyboard controls.
- Respect reduced motion and visibility. The shared activity gate suspends continuous work when the specimen is hidden, deactivated or unmounted.
- Use `TxTextMorph` for changing text values, `TxIconMorph` for vector stroke icons, and the shared spring engine for motion rather than stacking duplicate animation engines.

## API Reference

### Imports

```ts
import {
  TxCardSpread,
  TxCarousel3D,
  TxDistortionWave,
  TxFlipBook,
  TxFlipOverlay,
  TxFoldCorner,
  TxFusion,
  TxFusionSurface,
  TxIconMorph,
  TxKeyframeStrokeText,
  TxLiquid,
  TxMorph,
  TxMotion,
  TxMotionButton,
  TxMotionControl,
  TxMotionDock,
  TxMotionForm,
  TxMotionLoader,
  TxMotionMetric,
  TxMotionText,
  TxMotionTransition,
  TxPhysicsMotion,
  TxPixelField,
  TxStagger,
  TxTextMorph,
  TxTextTransformer,
  TxTransition,
  TxTuffLogoStroke,
  TxVoiceRing,
} from '@talex-touch/tuffex/pro'
import { TxDitherChart } from '@talex-touch/tuffex/charts'
import '@talex-touch/tuffex/base.css'
```

The `suite="motion"` key above is a documentation grouping; there is no fourth installation suite barrel. `@talex-touch/tuffex/motion` is the legal single-component subpath for `TxMotion`. For manual component imports, follow the on-demand stylesheet instructions on [Installation](/en/installation) and each component's API page.

